# TypeScript & Knex

- Keep `strict` TypeScript. Prefer explicit types on public service/model APIs.
- Validate request input with Zod at the controller edge; throw `AppError` subclasses from services.
- Use Knex only inside `src/models/**` (plus `src/db/**` setup/migrations).
- Prefer JSONB for nested assessment payload/report; do not flatten report fields into columns unless querying requires it.
- Use `ea_` + ULID for assessment ids via `src/utils/id.ts`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — query in controller
const row = await db("assessments").where({ id }).first();

// ✅ GOOD — controller → service → model
const report = await AssessmentService.getById(id);
```
